{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790347374,"nonce":"Mzrzm+Gu+m68/OFABDdLUHTk9lI=","title":"ZynML package manager","message":"A package manager for ZynML: a manifest naming a package, its version and its dependencies (ZynML packages and ZRTL plugins), version resolution with a lockfile, fetching from a registry or a git URL, and a build step that produces the package's ZPack.\n\nZPack (crates/compiler/src/zpack.rs, book/10-packaging-distribution.md) is already the distribution unit: an archive of compiled modules plus per-triple ZRTL libraries. What is missing is everything above it: no manifest format, no versioning, no resolver, no registry, and ZynML's module resolution does not look in an installed-packages location.\n\nThis is ZynML only; zypy uses pip and venvs, and zylua uses require paths.","files":null}]}